UID:pulitzer-center-global-south-civil-society-microgrants-2026@artificialn
 ouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260902T110337Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260906
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260907
SUMMARY:Deadline: Pulitzer Center: Global South Civil Society Microgrants 2
 026
DESCRIPTION:The Pulitzer Center funds civil society in the Global South to 
 build civic engagement projects around Pulitzer Center-supported journalis
 m: grassroots collectives\, community-led movements\, ARTISTS and civic co
 alitions taking published reporting to the communities it concerns. This g
 rant cycle is restricted to the Center's Climate and Environment topics: R
 AINFOREST (drivers of rainforest degradation\, the role of global markets\
 , finance and policy\, centring the rights and roles of Indigenous peoples
 )\, OCEAN (degradation of marine environments\, ocean health and the clima
 te crisis\, ocean governance\, science-backed and community-led solutions)
 \, and CLIMATE AND LABOR (the intersection of climate and labour\, includi
 ng gender\, livelihoods\, adaptation and community resilience). WHAT COUNT
 S AS A PROJECT: community engagement and organising that connects reportin
 g with audiences\; creative expressions\, explicitly including digital cam
 paigns\, public performances and creative publication formats\; public dia
 logues bringing together affected communities\, journalists\, decision-mak
 ers and academia\; and other innovative uses of the reporting that build o
 n local cultural practices. Every project must use at least one published 
 Pulitzer Center-supported reporting project meaningfully\, or involve a Pu
 litzer Center-supported journalist centrally\, and must name a clear targe
 t audience. OUT OF SCOPE: journalism and reporting projects themselves (th
 ose go to the Center's reporting grants)\, anything not built on Pulitzer 
 Center-supported reporting\, direct advocacy or lobbying\, campaigns endor
 sing political candidates or parties\, and for-profit projects. WHO CAN AP
 PLY: grassroots organisations\, community educators\, civil society organi
 sations and coalitions\, youth movements and other groups working at the i
 ntersection of journalism\, civic rights and active citizenship\, with pas
 t experience running civic engagement activities in the Global South\, pro
 ven experience on the named topics\, and the operational capacity to manag
 e a microgrant from an international organisation. APPLICATION: a project 
 description of no more than 400 words\, the target audience and desired im
 pact\, your methodology\, a timeline and budget\, the lead applicant's CV 
 with a letter of recommendation\, and\, where activities involve Indigenou
 s peoples or traditional communities\, a signed or recorded statement of c
 onsent from a community member. Applications are accepted in English\, Spa
 nish\, Portuguese\, French and Indonesian through Submittable. TIMELINE: a
 pplications 15 August to 6 September 2026\, selection announced mid-Septem
 ber 2026\, onboarding October 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Pulitzer Center\nLoca
 tion: Global South\, with the call naming Africa\, Latin America and South
 east Asia. Groups based in the United States apply to the separate U.S. Ci
 vil Society Microgrant instead.\nAward: USD 2\,000 to USD 4\,000 per proje
 ct. Applicants name the amount requested and submit a draft budget. Funds 
 are transferred to the partner after the agreement is signed\; partners fi
 le a financial narrative and outcomes report at the end but are NOT requir
 ed to collect detailed receipts. No application fee.\nDuration: Up to six 
 months of implementation\, October 2026 to March 2027\, with a virtual che
 ck-in in December 2026 and closure in early March 2027.\n\nMore: https://p
 ulitzercenter.org/opportunities/reporting-grants-fellowships/global-south-
 civil-society-microgrants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium
 =referral
URL:https://pulitzercenter.org/opportunities/reporting-grants-fellowships/g
 lobal-south-civil-society-microgrants?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Global South\, with the call naming Africa\, Latin America and Sou
 theast Asia. Groups based in the United States apply to the separate U.S. 
 Civil Society Microgrant instead.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:asian-cultural-council-individual-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.git
 hub.io
DTSTAMP:20260902T110337Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261111
SUMMARY:Deadline: Asian Cultural Council: Individual Fellowship 2027
DESCRIPTION:The Asian Cultural Council's Individual Fellowship funds artist
 s\, scholars and arts professionals from Asia and the U.S. to spend one to
  six months somewhere new or less familiar\, pursuing self-designed resear
 ch and cultural immersion: meeting practitioners\, visiting studios\, muse
 ums\, galleries\, theatres and libraries\, joining workshops and symposia\
 , and doing archival research. ACC is explicit that this is not a producti
 on residency\, not a conference travel grant and not a PR tour. APPLYING J
 OINTLY: two or three people who share research goals can apply together as
  equal partners (one primary applicant\, up to two co-applicants\, no assi
 stant roles)\; the USD 35\,000 cap covers the whole team. Applicants must 
 be citizens or legal permanent residents of an ACC-eligible country\, terr
 itory or region: Afghanistan\, Bangladesh\, Bhutan\, Brunei\, Cambodia\, C
 hina (Mainland)\, East Timor\, Hong Kong SAR\, India\, Indonesia\, Japan\,
  Korea\, Laos\, Macau SAR\, Malaysia\, Mongolia\, Myanmar\, Nepal\, Pakist
 an\, Philippines\, Singapore\, Sri Lanka\, Taiwan\, Thailand\, the U.S. an
 d Vietnam. ELIGIBLE DISCIPLINES (16): architecture (design\, history and t
 heory)\, archaeology\, art history\, arts administration\, arts criticism\
 , conservation\, crafts\, curation\, dance\, ethnomusicology\, film\, lite
 rature\, museum studies\, music\, theater and visual art\; video art and p
 hotography apply under visual art. Additional requirements: at least 21 ye
 ars old by the start\, at least five years of professional experience in a
 n eligible discipline\, no university coursework or teaching during the fe
 llowship\, and confident English if travelling to the U.S. on a J-1 visa. 
 Anyone who has held an ACC grant in the last two calendar years is ineligi
 ble. DESTINATIONS: any eligible country except the one you currently live 
 in\; a place you have lived in for over a year or hold citizenship in need
 s a strong rationale. U.S. fellowships need at least 30 consecutive days a
 nd cannot start before 1 October 2027 because of J-1 processing\; fellowsh
 ips in Asia need 30 cumulative days\, splittable into trips of at least 14
  consecutive days with no more than 14 days between them. ACC sponsors the
  J-1 for U.S. travel\; for Asia you arrange your own visas\, and the fees 
 can go in the budget. WHAT ACC WILL NOT FUND: this is strictly cultural-ex
 change and immersion funding\, not production money. Filming a documentary
 \, researching a planned book or film\, mounting an exhibition\, running a
  concert series\, promotional or PR travel\, equipment purchases and full-
 time residency programmes are all ineligible\, as is funding used only to 
 travel to a single event. TIMELINE: the portal opens 1 October 2026 at 9:5
 9am ET\, applications close 10 November 2026 at 9:59am ET\, and letters of
  recommendation are due 16 November 2026 at 9:59am ET. Review runs Novembe
 r 2026 to April 2027\, notifications go out mid-May 2027\, and all funded 
 activity must take place between 1 August 2027 and 31 December 2028. Apply
  through the GoApply portal\; ACC does not accept email applications. Appl
 icants may apply to only one ACC programme per cycle. No application fee.\
 n\nOrganisation: Asian Cultural Council (ACC)\nLocation: Travel between an
 d within Asia and the United States. Open to citizens and legal permanent 
 residents of ACC-eligible countries\, territories and regions\, including 
 the U.S. You cannot propose travel to the place where you currently live.\
 nAward: Up to USD 35\,000\, the same cap whether you apply alone or jointl
 y with up to two co-applicants. Covers economy airfare\, ground transport\
 , accommodation\, food and daily living costs\, visa fees\, mandatory trav
 el health insurance\, interpretation and costs tied to the exchange activi
 ties. Also included: ACC logistical and research guidance\, introductions 
 to alumni and professionals\, and visa assistance for U.S. travel. No appl
 ication fee.\nDuration: One to six months\, at least 30 days in the destin
 ation\; ACC prefers two months or more in a single place.\n\nMore: https:/
 /www.asianculturalcouncil.org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.asianculturalcouncil.org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Travel between and within Asia and the United States. Open to citi
 zens and legal permanent residents of ACC-eligible countries\, territories
  and regions\, including the U.S. You cannot propose travel to the place w
 here you currently live.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:asian-cultural-council-organization-grant-2027@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20260902T110337Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261111
SUMMARY:Deadline: Asian Cultural Council: Organization Grant 2027
DESCRIPTION:ACC's Organization Grant funds arts and culture organisations i
 n Asia and the U.S. to run cultural-exchange activities for their staff\, 
 communities and collaborators: sending an activity lead and participants a
 broad\, hosting incoming participants at home\, or both. Up to USD 50\,000
 \, set by ACC against the proposed budget\, activities\, travel duration a
 nd application quality. ELIGIBILITY: the applicant must be a nonprofit\, a
  government-affiliated or sponsored arts or cultural institution (national
  museums\, performing arts centres and the like)\, or an academic or highe
 r-education institution\; legally registered and based in an ACC-eligible 
 country\, territory or region\; and have at least five years of artistic o
 r cultural programming experience. Each application names a primary contac
 t\, an activity lead who runs the work on the ground (can be the same pers
 on)\, and activity participants who may be staff or external collaborators
 . The lead and all participants must be citizens or legal permanent reside
 nts of an eligible location\, and they do not have to share a nationality 
 with each other or with the organisation. Applicants must be citizens or l
 egal permanent residents of an ACC-eligible country\, territory or region:
  Afghanistan\, Bangladesh\, Bhutan\, Brunei\, Cambodia\, China (Mainland)\
 , East Timor\, Hong Kong SAR\, India\, Indonesia\, Japan\, Korea\, Laos\, 
 Macau SAR\, Malaysia\, Mongolia\, Myanmar\, Nepal\, Pakistan\, Philippines
 \, Singapore\, Sri Lanka\, Taiwan\, Thailand\, the U.S. and Vietnam. ELIGI
 BLE DISCIPLINES (16): architecture (design\, history and theory)\, archaeo
 logy\, art history\, arts administration\, arts criticism\, conservation\,
  crafts\, curation\, dance\, ethnomusicology\, film\, literature\, museum 
 studies\, music\, theater and visual art\; video art and photography apply
  under visual art. TRAVEL: one to six months within the grant period\, at 
 least 30 consecutive days in the U.S. or 30 cumulative days in Asia (split
 table into trips of at least 14 consecutive days\, no more than 14 days ap
 art). Travel to a place the lead or participants have spent over a year in
  needs a strong rationale\, and multi-destination or short itineraries are
  less competitive. ACC does not sponsor visas for this programme\; the org
 anisation secures them. WHAT ACC WILL NOT FUND: this is strictly cultural-
 exchange and immersion funding\, not production money. Filming a documenta
 ry\, researching a planned book or film\, mounting an exhibition\, running
  a concert series\, promotional or PR travel\, equipment purchases and ful
 l-time residency programmes are all ineligible\, as is funding used only t
 o travel to a single event. TIMELINE: the portal opens 1 October 2026 at 9
 :59am ET\, applications close 10 November 2026 at 9:59am ET\, and letters 
 of recommendation are due 16 November 2026 at 9:59am ET. Review runs Novem
 ber 2026 to April 2027\, notifications go out mid-May 2027\, and all funde
 d activity must take place between 1 August 2027 and 31 December 2028. App
 ly through the GoApply portal\; ACC does not accept email applications. Ap
 plicants may apply to only one ACC programme per cycle. No application fee
 .\n\nOrganisation: Asian Cultural Council (ACC)\nLocation: Asia and the Un
 ited States. The applicant organisation must be legally registered and bas
 ed in an ACC-eligible country\, territory or region\; activity leads and p
 articipants must be citizens or permanent residents of an eligible locatio
 n\, not necessarily the same one as the organisation.\nAward: Up to USD 50
 \,000. Covers economy airfare\, ground transport\, accommodation\, food an
 d daily living costs\, visa fees\, mandatory travel health insurance\, int
 erpretation and costs tied to the exchange activities. Also included: ACC 
 logistical and substantive guidance\, introductions to alumni\, arts profe
 ssionals and institutions\, and invitations to local ACC events. No applic
 ation fee.\nDuration: One to six months of travel\; at least 30 consecutiv
 e days for U.S. activity\, or 30 cumulative days in Asia.\n\nMore: https:/
 /www.asianculturalcouncil.org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.asianculturalcouncil.org/grant-opportunities?utm_source=art
 ificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Asia and the United States. The applicant organisation must be leg
 ally registered and based in an ACC-eligible country\, territory or region
 \; activity leads and participants must be citizens or permanent residents
  of an eligible location\, not necessarily the same one as the organisatio
 n.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a4-residency-chengdu-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260902T110337Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261231
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
SUMMARY:Deadline: A4 Residency Art Center: International Residency Programm
 e 2028 (Chengdu)
DESCRIPTION:Multidisciplinary international residency at the A4 Residency A
 rt Center in Chengdu\, China\, a global exchange platform integrating crea
 tion\, networking and resources\, dedicated to fostering cross-cultural cr
 eative collisions and innovation through residency programmes while promot
 ing deep integration of creative culture with commerce and communities. Re
 sidents initiate one to two participatory local activities to facilitate c
 ommunication with the city and community\; A4 also organises group activit
 ies\, intimate sharing and exhibition opportunities to foster understandin
 g among creators and connect them with local resources. AVAILABLE DATES: S
 pring 2028 (April - June) or Autumn 2028 (July - October). ELIGIBILITY: in
 ternational applicants from any field\; A4 welcomes applications from mult
 idisciplinary artists (visual\, performing\, music\, film\, sound\, archit
 ecture)\, curators\, designers (product\, fashion\, spatial\, interactive)
 \, and interdisciplinary creatives. PROGRAMME SUPPORT: studio and accommod
 ation\; round-trip economy airfare or 2nd-class train within a set budget\
 ; RMB 10\,000 production grant per person/team (excluding living expenses)
 . DEADLINE: 31 December 2026 (2028 cycles). APPLY via the A4 Residency Art
  Center latest-recruitment page.\n\nOrganisation: A4 Residency Art Center 
 (A4 Art Museum)\nLocation: Chengdu\, China\nAward: Studio and accommodatio
 n provided\; round-trip economy airfare or second-class train ticket withi
 n a set budget\; production grant of RMB 10\,000 per person/team for creat
 ive production and material costs (excluding living expenses). No applicat
 ion fee.\nDuration: No less than 8 weeks during one of two 2028 cycles: Sp
 ring 2028 (April - June) or Autumn 2028 (July - October)\n\nMore: https://
 www.a4artmuseum.com/en/a4-residencyartcenter/residing/latest-recruitment/?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.a4artmuseum.com/en/a4-residencyartcenter/residing/latest-re
 cruitment/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Chengdu\, China
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
